WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.600
The James River starts as fresh water in Virginia's mountains.

2
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.900
It ends in the salty Chesapeake Bay.

3
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.580
Wild oyster reefs grow in the lower river.

4
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.920
Near Richmond, the water is fresh, and oysters can die.

5
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:26.420
So why do different living things live in a mountain stream, a forest, and the salty Bay?

7
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.130
Every place has an ecosystem.

8
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:35.490
An ecosystem is all the living things in a place, together with their nonliving

9
00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:39.570
surroundings. The living parts are biotic factors.

10
00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.790
A deer eating acorns is biotic.

11
00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:46.610
The nonliving parts are abiotic factors.

12
00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:51.410
Sunlight, water, soil, and air are abiotic.

13
00:00:52.283 --> 00:00:57.483
Abiotic factors help decide which organisms can survive in a place.

14
00:00:58.503 --> 00:01:02.083
Few plants can grow on a forest floor that gets little sunlight.

15
00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.463
Water and floating mud block light.

16
00:01:05.963 --> 00:01:09.763
So few plants grow on the floor of deep or muddy water.

17
00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:14.827
Scientists sort ecosystems into three broad groups.

18
00:01:15.627 --> 00:01:18.807
A terrestrial ecosystem is on land, like a forest.

19
00:01:19.707 --> 00:01:24.667
A freshwater ecosystem has water with very little salt, like a mountain stream.

20
00:01:25.587 --> 00:01:28.467
A marine ecosystem has salty ocean water.

21
00:01:29.547 --> 00:01:32.387
Salinity is the amount of salt dissolved in water.

22
00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:35.817
Now follow the James downstream.

23
00:01:37.057 --> 00:01:42.117
An estuary is a place where fresh river water mixes with salty ocean water.

24
00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:44.897
The Chesapeake Bay is an estuary.

25
00:01:45.777 --> 00:01:49.757
Its salinity is in between, and it shifts with rain and season.

26
00:01:50.817 --> 00:01:54.057
As the river flows toward the Bay, salinity rises.

27
00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:57.127
Now think about the oysters.

28
00:01:58.347 --> 00:02:03.147
Eastern oysters can die when the water stays very low in salt for a long time.

29
00:02:04.127 --> 00:02:07.107
Brackish water is in between fresh and salty.

30
00:02:08.207 --> 00:02:10.907
Oyster reefs grow in the brackish lower James.

31
00:02:11.727 --> 00:02:14.927
The fresh water near Richmond is poor oyster habitat.

32
00:02:15.707 --> 00:02:19.387
So why do different living things live in different places?

33
00:02:20.447 --> 00:02:25.757
Abiotic factors such as salt and sunlight, together with the living things, decide

34
00:02:25.757 --> 00:02:27.617
who lives in each ecosystem.
